.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="PolynomialRegression fits a degree-``d`` polynomial by solving the normal equations V^T V c = V^T y. This script fits noisy cubic data, checks the R^2 and residuals, and then shows the fit&#x27;s condition number (estimated via power iteration on the normal-equations matrix) growing sharply with degree -- squaring the design matrix&#x27;s own condition number is exactly why the normal-equations approach is eventually replaced by a QR-based least-squares solve in mathematicskit.linalg.">

